Subject: [PATCH 02499/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE C1
 (IN-GENERATION ACCURACY moat; REPAIR-OR-RETIRE) -- the DiffusionGemma
 moat->generation conversion has blocked 3x on DIFFERENT measurement failures
 (.399 degenerate-controls -> .402 MCQ-harness-bug -> .403
 scorer_leaky_in_search_corpus). .404 gives it ONE disciplined attempt with a
 CLEAN EXIT, mapped by the SOTA-ingestion: (1) REQUALIFY the .401 leak-robust
 scorer (exp4337 .pkl) leak-robustness ON the free-form GENERATION corpus (the
 .403 leak was corpus-specific -- the scorer recovers answer cells from
 position cues on the generation canvas); (2) add a scorer-INDEPENDENT
 local-coherence control (CoDiLA arXiv:2603.20216 -- a small local AR verifier
 / deterministic block-coherence penalty that needs NO external scorer) so the
 in-generation arms are MEASURABLE without the leaky scorer; (3) PAPO
 (arXiv:2606.08501) reward-state diagnostic; THEN the fixed-NFE Prism search
 (arXiv:2602.01842 HTS + partial-remask branching) vs DIFFERENTIATED controls
 (unguided, best-of-N@matched-NFE, intrinsic self-verified-feedback) OR a
 clean RETIREMENT. Skeptic-proof by construction: the no-op
 DEGENERATE_CONTROLS guard, a metric-TAUTOLOGY guard, the independent leak
 re-check, branch-diversity receipts, scorer-disagreement rows. Emit
 s3_guided_beats_control BARE bool (true iff the repaired-scorer OR the
 CoDiLA-control-grounded search beats best-of-N@NFE AND intrinsic-SVF,
 CI95-excl-0, controls_differentiated). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = the
 moat graduates 'exists'->'useful'; a CLEAN differentiated null = the
 in-generation scale-up retires; if the scorer leaks AGAIN after
 corpus-specific requalification AND CoDiLA ALSO cannot differentiate the arms
 -> the in-generation-conversion-via-this-scorer direction RETIRES (4th block,
 falsifiable). NO TRM training; DiffusionGemma via the llama.cpp PR binary.

